<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Wave 03 "PRIME": the ribbon of past drops returns to the board, in the `carousel` edition
      (DESIGN §7.5, §10.2).

      Drops travel as a vertical ribbon, and the main one is the one that lands in the MIDDLE of the window: a frame's look is
      a pure function of its distance to the middle, and the layout is not recalculated at all.
      So the tile behaves the same with three drops and with three hundred, and the archive pages
      endlessly in both directions.

      The path to this look took two rounds of prototypes on the live canvas, and both are worth remembering.
      The first was expanding a frame on hover (archive spines): it hits a wall that cannot
      be bypassed by tweaking numbers, because an expanded frame takes space from the column:
      "cover ≤ window − 32 × neighbours", i.e. 137px with four drops and 41px with seven.
      The second round was already shot with scrolling as the mechanism (film · carousel · slots ·
      spread · scrubber); the owner chose the carousel.

      Geometry. The column stands between the latest drop's frame and the Spotify plate, right next to
      the photo it grew out of. For it the cluster was rebuilt: the frame moved left (10 → 5),
      music and the switcher right (22 → 27, 24 → 29), and the board is centred on the 40x28 grid
      again (5..36 with the centre at 21). The column itself is raised to the canvas's TOP edge (row 3): in
      the middle of the grid it shared its height with the frame and read as a second identical column.

      Size: 8 tracks wide by 9 high. The slot height is fixed (83px), so the number
      of visible frames is set not by the archive but by the tile: two and a half fit in its window, and the third,
      cut off at the bottom, is exactly the hint that the ribbon goes on.

      `orientation` is not set on purpose: the carousel's layout is vertical by nature,
      and the tile drops the orientation itself. Waves 01 and 02 have no `edition` field and stay on
      the old ribbons (the code default).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0630-wave-03-drop-carousel" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(
                jsonb_set(
                    jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,photoDrops}', $J${"col": 17, "row": 3, "colSpan": 8, "rowSpan": 9, "edition": "carousel"}$J$::jsonb),
                    '{tiles,latestDrop}',
                    $J${"col": 5, "row": 6, "colSpan": 11, "rowSpan": 16, "edition": "frame"}$J$::jsonb
                ),
                '{tiles,music}',
                $J${"col": 27, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 6}$J$::jsonb
            ),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 29, "row": 16, "colSpan": 6, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["music", "latestDrop", "photoDrops", "waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(
                jsonb_set(
                    jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,photoDrops}', $J${"hidden": true}$J$::jsonb),
                    '{tiles,latestDrop}',
                    $J${"col": 10, "row": 6, "colSpan": 11, "rowSpan": 16, "edition": "frame"}$J$::jsonb
                ),
                '{tiles,music}',
                $J${"col": 22, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 6}$J$::jsonb
            ),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 24, "row": 16, "colSpan": 6, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["music", "latestDrop", "waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
